---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="For site hosts | ChargeVia by Rangeway"
  description="Explore hosting ChargeVia by Rangeway at an existing retail, fuel, or hospitality property with easy access, useful amenities, and care for visitors.">
  <main id="main" class="detail-page shell">
    <header class="detail-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">For site hosts</p>
        <h1>You bring the place.<br />We bring the charge.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="detail-heading__intro">For retailers and property owners with a place worth stopping. Let’s explore how ChargeVia by Rangeway could fit alongside your business.</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="concept-frame concept-frame--orange hosts-concept">
      <img src="/images/cv-retail-1672.webp"
        srcset="/images/cv-retail-640.webp 640w, /images/cv-retail-960.webp 960w, /images/cv-retail-1672.webp 1672w"
        sizes="(min-width: 1500px) 1376px, (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 112px), calc(100vw - 56px)"
        alt="Concept rendering of fast charging beside an existing retail storefront with outdoor seating"
        width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high" />
      <figcaption>Concept rendering. A site’s layout would depend on the property.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="editorial-section property-fit" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
      <header>
        <p class="section-label">A good fit starts here</p>
        <h2 id="fit-title">The place matters<br />as much as the plug.</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Retail, fuel, and hospitality properties can all be part of the conversation. We’re looking at the whole stop.</p>
      </header>
      <dl class="property-list">
        <div><dt>Easy access</dt><dd>A property that’s straightforward to reach, enter, and move around.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Useful amenities</dt><dd>Food, drinks, restrooms, or something useful to do while charging. The right mix depends on the property.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Care for the place</dt><dd>Clean, well-maintained surroundings and a host who pays attention to visitors.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="operating-story" aria-labelledby="roles-title">
      <header>
        <p class="section-label">Working together</p>
        <h2 id="roles-title">Your business.<br />Our charging.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="operating-story__roles">
        <div><h3>Rangeway’s role</h3><p>Rangeway would develop and manage the charging operation and the ChargeVia customer experience.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Your role</h3><p>You keep running the business your customers know, with the amenities and care that make your property a useful stop.</p></div>
        <p class="concept-status">Each property would need its own review. Site fit, scope, and responsibilities would be agreed before a project moves forward.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="host-invitation" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
      <h2 id="contact-title">Have a place in mind?</h2>
      <div>
        <p>Tell us a little about your business, the property, and the amenities already there. That’s a good place to start.</p>
        <a class="host-contact" href="mailto:partners@rangeway.co"><span>partners@rangeway.co</span><span aria-hidden="true">»</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
